12	// The tests of the upstream cut (DEVDESK-534, NX-02b, step 2):
13	//
14	//	CutUpstream(ctx, runner, clock, p, out) error
15	//
16	// against the scripted kubectl of upstream_test.go (upstreamKubectl, whose rounds
17	// play before the scale is accepted and after it) and the fake clock of
18	// clock_test.go. No real kubectl, no real wait, nothing on a cluster.
19	//
20	// Like EnsureUpstream, CutUpstream runs no preflight: the command runs OpCut
21	// first. The kubectl calls the tests assume (arguments after "kubectl", without
22	// --context; "--request-timeout=<d>" is ignored):
23	//
24	//	get deployment bench-upstream -n <ns> -o json        (the read)
25	//	scale deployment/bench-upstream --replicas=0 -n <ns> (the only write)
26	//	get pods -n <ns> -l app.kubernetes.io/name=bench-upstream -o json
27	//	                                                     (the wait, once per round)
28	//
29	// Choices of the tests, to settle with the code:
30	//   - It reads first. Ready or Starting: one scale to zero, then the wait. Cut:
31	//     no write, and the wait still runs (a pod of a previous cut may be
32	//     terminating). Missing: an error, no write, no wait.
33	//   - The wait lists the pods of the upstream, sleeps upstreamPollInterval
34	//     between two rounds, and ends on the first round with NO pod at all: a pod
35	//     that is terminating counts (its volume is still mounted).
36	//   - It gives up at p.Timeout (within one interval) with a Deadline that names
37	//     the pods still there and NEXUS_BENCH_TIMEOUT.
38	//   - A failed scale is classified (classifyKubectl) and never retried.
39	//   - A custom upstream URL is refused before any call. A cancelled context is
40	//     returned as is. A nil writer is accepted.
41	//
42	// What step 0 (H-CUTDELAY) may change: nothing here. The wait is on the
43	// cluster, not on the proxy.
44	
45	// goingPod is a pod of the upstream that is shutting down.
46	func goingPod(name string) upPod {
47		return upPod{fakePod: fakePod{name: name, phase: "Running", scheduled: "True", running: true, ready: true}, terminating: true}
48	}
49	
50	// goingRound is the upstream at zero replicas with the pods still shutting down.
51	func goingRound(pods ...upPod) upstreamRound {
52		return upstreamRound{deployment: true, replicas: 0, pods: pods, claim: "Bound"}
53	}
